From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Generate a real door image: text step then image step, for every column

Generate in the door editor is one pipeline run three times. Every column does
the same two steps, and the final output of every column is the image:

  step 1  the column's provider reads the door photo and record and writes a
          detailed text description of the door
  step 2  an image model draws a photo-accurate door image from that
          description, using the same door photo as its reference

  GPT     step 1 GPT        step 2 OpenAI images
  Gemini  step 1 Gemini     step 2 Gemini images
  Claude  step 1 Claude     step 2 Gemini images

Claude is a text writer in this pipeline, not a special case. Anthropic's
Messages API returns text only, so its description drives the image model the
backend already runs for room scenes. That is the design.

Claude model
------------
The default is now claude-sonnet-5-5, an Active Sonnet-class model (released
2026-09-28, retirement not sooner than 2027-09-28). It replaces
claude-sonnet-4-5, which Anthropic deprecated on 2026-09-30 and retires on
2026-11-30. Still overridable with ANTHROPIC_DOOR_DESCRIPTION_MODEL, and no
value has to be set: the default works as shipped.

Because current Sonnet-class models think adaptively by default at `high`
effort and thinking counts against max_tokens, a budget sized for the answer
alone can be spent entirely on thinking and come back empty with
stop_reason "max_tokens". The Claude request now asks for max_tokens 4096
and output_config.effort "low", which is ample to read a door photograph and
write ten labelled lines.

The other two columns
---------------------
GPT previously sent max_completion_tokens to a chat-completions model.
OpenAI documents max_tokens as deprecated in favour of max_completion_tokens
and says it "is not compatible with o-series models"; sending the wrong one
is a 400. The field is now chosen from the model id: max_completion_tokens
for the o1/o3/o4/gpt-5 reasoning families, max_tokens for the rest.

No column could ever return an image before: nothing in either provider call
asked for one, and the tile under a generated description was a local vector
sketch badged "Library default".

Diagnostics
-----------
Every failure is now logged with the provider, status, model id and a
redacted provider body, under [ai-door-describe] and [ai-door-image]. Before
this, a failed call returned one generic sentence and logged nothing.

Storage and keys
----------------
Drawn images go to door-style-images/ai-generated/ and are served by the
storage proxy. Keys are unchanged and stay server-side. Optional variables
with working defaults, so nothing has to be set:
  OPENAI_DOOR_IMAGE_MODEL   default gpt-image-2
  GEMINI_IMAGE_MODEL        default gemini-3.1-flash-image

Tests: server/lib/aiDoorImage.test.ts (13), server/lib/aiDoorDescribe.test.ts
(26), server/lib/aiDoorDescribe.wiring.test.ts (7). tsc --noEmit reports no
errors in these files.

